\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Faith of our fathers, living still
\par In spite of dungeon, fire, and sword,
\par O how our hearts beat high  with joy
\par Whene'er we hear that glorious word.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Faith of our fathers! Holy faith!
\par We will be true to thee till death.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our fathers, chained in prisons dark,
\par Were still in heart and conscience free;
\par And blest would be their children's fate,
\par Though they, like them, should die for thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Faith of our fathers! Holy faith!
\par We will be true to thee till death.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Faith of our fathers! God's great power
\par Shall soon all nations win for thee;
\par And through the truth that comes from God
\par Mankind shall  then indeed be free.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Faith of our fathers! Holy faith!
\par We will be true to thee till death.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Faith of our fathers! We will  love
\par Both friend and foe in all our strife,
\par And preach thee, too, as love knows how,
\par By kindly words and virtuous life:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Faith of our fathers! Holy faith!
\par We will be true to thee till death.
\par \f1 
